{#
  The privacy policy's "Ads" section (cfpa/ads.py, docs/adr/0040), included
  by privacy.html.jinja only when ads are on. The "Turn off ads" button sets
  the same localStorage flag that _ad_slot.html.jinja reads before it loads
  anything from Google.
#}
<h2 id="ads">Ads</h2>
<p>
  Since {{ ads_effective_date }}, some pages on this website show one ad from
  Google AdSense: the water, county, region, species and past-week pages, and
  the other states&rsquo; pages. It sits at the end of the page, under the
  label &ldquo;Advertisement&rdquo;. Google, not this site, chooses the ad,
  and the site&rsquo;s owner earns money when ads are shown or clicked. The
  ad is separate from the gear links above, which are links this site
  chose.
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Non-personalized ads only.</strong> The site asks Google for
      non-personalized ads, which are chosen from the page&rsquo;s content and
      your approximate location (about city level), not from your past
      browsing. Google still uses cookies or similar storage for these ads,
      to limit how often you see the same ad, to count ads in aggregate and
      to stop fraud. Google&rsquo;s script, from googlesyndication.com, loads
      only on the pages listed above.</li>
  <li><strong>Restricted data processing.</strong> The site&rsquo;s AdSense
      account uses Google&rsquo;s restricted data processing for visitors from
      US states with privacy laws, including California. Google then acts as
      this site&rsquo;s service provider for the ad data and does not build or
      use advertising profiles from it.</li>
  <li><strong>Do Not Sell or Share.</strong> This site does not sell or share
      your personal information, as those terms are used in California
      privacy law. You can still turn the ads off on this device:</li>
  <li><strong>Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track are honored.</strong>
      If your browser sends either signal, the ad script is never loaded:
      nothing is requested from Google for ads and no ad cookie is set.</li>
  <li id="ads-opt-out"><strong>Turning ads off on this device.</strong> The
      button below saves that choice in this browser&rsquo;s local storage for
      this site, not in a cookie, and it is never sent anywhere. Every page
      checks it before loading the ad script. Press the button again to undo
      it. Ad cookies Google set before you turned ads off stay in your browser
      until they expire or you clear them.
      <span id="ads-choice" hidden><button type="button" id="ads-toggle" class="link-button">Turn off ads</button> <span id="ads-status" role="status"></span></span></li>
  <li><strong>The EEA, the UK and Switzerland:</strong> Google&rsquo;s own
      consent message asks before any ad cookie is set there.</li>
  <li><strong>Where there are never ads:</strong> the home page, the
      &ldquo;What to bring&rdquo; page, the about, privacy, support and data
      pages, the guides, any email from this site, and the iPhone and Android
      apps.</li>
  <li><strong>No ad, no box.</strong> If Google has no ad for a page, or the
      ad is blocked, nothing is shown in its place.</li>
  <li><strong>Google&rsquo;s terms:</strong>
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how
      Google uses information from sites that use its services</a> and
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">how Google uses
      cookies in advertising</a>.</li>
</ul>
<script>
(function () {
  var w = window, d = document, key = "trout-truck:ads-opt-out";
  d.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", function () {
    var box = d.getElementById("ads-choice");
    var button = d.getElementById("ads-toggle");
    var status = d.getElementById("ads-status");
    if (!box || !button || !status) return;
    var off = false;
    try { off = w.localStorage.getItem(key) === "1"; } catch (e) {}
    function show(message) {
      button.textContent = off ? "Turn ads back on" : "Turn off ads";
      status.textContent = message;
    }
    box.hidden = false;
    show(off ? "Ads are off on this device." : "");
    button.addEventListener("click", function () {
      off = !off;
      try {
        if (off) w.localStorage.setItem(key, "1");
        else w.localStorage.removeItem(key);
      } catch (e) {
        off = !off;
        show("Your browser would not save this choice. Global Privacy Control turns ads off without it.");
        return;
      }
      show(off ? "Ads are off on this device." : "Ads are back on from the next page you open.");
    });
  });
})();
</script>
